@startbpmn BP01_StartBearing_Blocks
lang en

output L1 "BP01_StartBearing.bpmn"

' The BLOCK VIEW of BP01: the process as the building blocks it is made of, one box per block
' instance, with no block internals. What is inside each box is 00_Path-Patterns.md's; the detailed
' levels are 01_detailed and 02_detailed. BP01 is one block whole. Hand-authored from the one
' tagged source in ../diagrams/, and re-read whenever that process changes.

pool "User" {
  start "Something to plan or do"
  :BB19 Launch · the data folder resolved, where the launch lands, or a refusal the user acknowledges;
  note "Launch is a whole-process shape, so BP01 is this one block: the preconditions, the folder, the landing tab and the close that follows a refused start-up are all inside it."
  end "Bearing in use, or ready to relaunch"
}

@endbpmn
